WARNING:DT_SPLIT_BINDING_PATCH: DT binding docs and includes should be a separate patch. See: Documentation/devicetree/bindings/submitting-patches.rst

Devicetree bindings should be their own patch.  This is because
bindings are logically independent from a driver implementation,
they have a different maintainer (even though they often
are applied via the same tree), and it makes for a cleaner history in the
DT only tree created with git-filter-branch.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/devicetree/bindings/submitting-patches.html#i-for-patch-submitters

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around '!pdat'
#146: FILE: drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c:64:
+	if ((!pdat) && pdev->dev.of_node) {

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*pdat)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct i2c_designware_platform_data)...)
#149: FILE: drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-designware-platdrv.c:67:
+		pdat = kmalloc(sizeof(struct i2c_designware_platform_data),

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

